#: rc.cpp:9 rc.cpp:10
msgid "Certificate Wizard"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:11
msgid ""
"<b>Welcome to the Certificate Wizard!</b>\n"
"<br>\n"
"<br>\n"
"In a few easy steps, this wizard will help you to create a certificate. You "
"use your certificates in order to sign messages, to encrypt messages and to "
"decrypt messages that other people send to you in encrypted form.\n"
"<p>\n"
"The certificates will be generated in a decentralized manner. Please contact "
"your local help desk if you are unsure how to create a certificate in your "
"organization."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:12
msgid "Your Personal Data"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:13
msgid ""
"On this page, you will enter some personal data that will be stored in your "
"certificate and that will help other people to determine that it is actually "
"you who is sending a message."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:14
msgid "&Name:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:15
msgid "Enter your name here"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:16
msgid "Enter your name here as it should be shown in the certificate."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:17
msgid "&Location:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:18
msgid "&Organization:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:19
msgid "Enter your organization here"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:20
msgid ""
"Enter your organization (e.g., your company, your department, or your "
"authority) here as it should appear on the certificate."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:21
msgid "&Department:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:22
msgid "&Country code:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:23
msgid "&Email address:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:24
msgid "Enter your email address here"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:25
msgid ""
"Enter the email address here which you want to use in connection with the "
"certificate."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:26
msgid "Decentralized Certificate Generation"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:27
msgid ""
"On this page, you will create a certificate in a decentralized way. You can "
"either store the certificate in a file for later transmission or send it to "
"the Certificate Authority (CA) directly. Please check with your local help "
"desk if you are unsure what to select here.<br>Once you are done with your "
"settings, click <em>Generate Certificate</em> in order to generate your "
"certificate."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:28
msgid "Certificate &Generation"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:29
msgid "&Store in a file"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:30
msgid "Send to CA as an &email message"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:31
msgid "&Generate Certificate"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:32
msgid "Your Certificate Is Ready To Be Sent"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:33
msgid ""
"<qt>\n"
"Your signature key pair is now ready to be sent to the CA (certification "
"authority) which will generate a certificate for you and send it back via "
"email (unless you have selected storage in a file). Please review the "
"certificate shown below.\n"
"<p>\n"
"If you want to change anything, press Back and make your changes. Otherwise "
"press Finish to send the signature key pair to the CA.\n"
"</qt>"
msgstr ""
